<title>USA: PG&amp;E Diablo 2 nuclear unit at 100 percent.</title>
<headline>PG&amp;E Diablo 2 nuclear unit at 100 percent.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pacific Gas and Electric Co's 1,073 megawatt (MW) Diablo Canyon 2 nuclear unit has resumed full power after being to reduced to about 82 percent over the weekend, Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The unit, in Avila Beach, Calif., was reduced due to a &quot;light system load.&quot;</p>
<p>The adjacent unit, with a generating capacity of 1,087 MW, is still operating at full power, the NRC said in its morning status report.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
